WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:02.729
- I've always believed
in following my dreams.

00:00:02.729 --> 00:00:04.660
- I like to go instinctively.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.361
If I love something, I want to do it.

00:00:06.361 --> 00:00:09.194
(loud rock music)

00:00:13.999 --> 00:00:14.832
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:16.323
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:16.323 --> 00:00:17.616
My one word is believe,

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:19.543
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:19.543 --> 00:00:21.806
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:21.806 --> 00:00:23.011
So, to help you on your journey today,

00:00:23.011 --> 00:00:25.504
we're going to learn from
Indian actor, director,

00:00:25.504 --> 00:00:28.040
and producer Aamir Khan and my take

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.476
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:30.476 --> 00:00:32.176
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:33.407
and I'd love to know which one

00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:34.851
you guys like the best.

00:00:34.851 --> 00:00:36.170
And as always, as you're watching,

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.238
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.040
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.468
Put quotes around it so other people

00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:42.385
can be inspired.

00:00:42.385 --> 00:00:44.101
Might win a prize, as well.

00:00:44.101 --> 00:00:45.664
And, also, when you write it down,

00:00:45.664 --> 00:00:48.611
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself, as well.

00:00:48.611 --> 00:00:49.444
Enjoy!

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:55.534
(motivational music)

00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:04.879
- And I think each one of us, you know,

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:06.651
finds their own path.

00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:09.318
So, what is the important to me,

00:01:10.168 --> 00:01:11.390
which I would like to share with you

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:12.882
is that I've always believed

00:01:12.882 --> 00:01:15.007
in following my dreams.

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:17.924
And I don't know how that happened.

00:01:19.453 --> 00:01:20.910
I'm not quite sure how that happened.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.946
But I think it also happened because

00:01:23.946 --> 00:01:25.834
I'm very passionate

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:26.817
about whatever I do.

00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:28.693
Whether it's my work, which is films.

00:01:28.693 --> 00:01:29.622
Whether it's playing a sport.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.017
Whether it's you know, hanging out

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:31.925
with my friends.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.213
Whether it's having an argument.

00:01:33.213 --> 00:01:34.588
Whether it's you know,

00:01:34.588 --> 00:01:35.421
laughing about something.

00:01:35.421 --> 00:01:36.882
I'm very passionate about everything.

00:01:36.882 --> 00:01:41.099
And I give my entire attention and full...

00:01:41.099 --> 00:01:42.434
Everything about me is in

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:43.772
that one thing that I'm doing

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:44.855
at that time.

00:01:47.225 --> 00:01:49.554
So, I think that what
is being very important

00:01:49.554 --> 00:01:52.430
for me is that I don't want to compromise

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.324
with what I want to do.

00:01:53.324 --> 00:01:55.141
What is my dream?

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:58.380
I don't mind compromising
to achieve my dream,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.739
but I don't want to
compromise the dream itself.

00:02:01.739 --> 00:02:04.104
So that is something that
I've always believed in.

00:02:04.104 --> 00:02:05.354
- I think that,

00:02:06.795 --> 00:02:08.767
what Gandhi said is so true.

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.995
That, be the change that you want to see.

00:02:11.995 --> 00:02:13.328
And I think that

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:19.382
each one of us can at
least change yourself.

00:02:19.382 --> 00:02:22.276
And that, itself, is such a big force

00:02:22.276 --> 00:02:24.109
in changing the world.

00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:26.072
- You know, you wake up in the morning,

00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:27.791
you read the papers, the news.

00:02:27.791 --> 00:02:28.680
You read about injustice.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.513
You read about poverty.

00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:31.366
You read about people who are

00:02:31.366 --> 00:02:32.614
less privileged than you.

00:02:32.614 --> 00:02:35.377
And you want to really
do something about it.

00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:36.746
I think most of us feel that way,

00:02:36.746 --> 00:02:37.986
and we don't know what to do.

00:02:37.986 --> 00:02:39.866
And I felt that for a number of years.

00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:43.455
And then I realized that I should do

00:02:43.455 --> 00:02:47.469
what I know best, which is storytelling.

00:02:47.469 --> 00:02:50.465
And I should use the
strength of storytelling

00:02:50.465 --> 00:02:54.947
to try and change minds
and try and, you know,

00:02:54.947 --> 00:02:58.887
enrich, perhaps, the
discussion on certain issues

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:00.750
that we face as a society.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.090
And I saw the ones really doing it

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.213
on that kind of a scale,

00:03:04.213 --> 00:03:06.595
on a public platform.

00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:09.158
And I thought if I
combine the strength of TV

00:03:09.158 --> 00:03:10.958
with the good will that I've earned,

00:03:10.958 --> 00:03:12.611
And you know, we try and...

00:03:12.611 --> 00:03:15.278
Actually, combine journalism,
investigative journalism

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:17.446
and storytelling.

00:03:17.446 --> 00:03:19.472
So we really research each topic,

00:03:19.472 --> 00:03:22.962
and then bring it to the country of India

00:03:22.962 --> 00:03:25.652
and share what we have
learned with the people.

00:03:25.652 --> 00:03:28.330
And hope that we can transform

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.873
minds, hearts.

00:03:29.873 --> 00:03:31.591
You know, I've always
felt that there's two ways

00:03:31.591 --> 00:03:33.545
of bringing about change.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:35.116
One is top-down.

00:03:35.116 --> 00:03:36.649
When you make laws

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.218
and you tell people to follow them.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.740
Or you make policies and you
expect people to follow them.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.790
And sometimes it works, but
a lot of time it doesn't.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.817
I think the other way is a longer route,

00:03:46.817 --> 00:03:49.561
but I think that is what
we have chosen to do.

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:53.642
And that is to reach
out to people's hearts.

00:03:53.642 --> 00:03:56.142
Not with anger, but with love.

00:03:57.405 --> 00:04:00.572
And, you know, try and transform minds

00:04:02.282 --> 00:04:03.470
at a young age.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.840
- [Interviewer] What is the
founder of your success?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:07.916
- Uh, I don't know, actually.

00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:09.278
I'm not quite aware

00:04:09.278 --> 00:04:12.195
of why I've been successful so far.

00:04:14.541 --> 00:04:17.026
You know I don't think so much about that.

00:04:17.026 --> 00:04:19.391
What I like to do is enjoy my work.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:21.533
So I do work which excites me.

00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:23.988
And often it's work
which, on the face of it

00:04:23.988 --> 00:04:25.905
is not considered very,

00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:29.313
you know, doesn't have the potential

00:04:29.313 --> 00:04:30.788
to be a big blockbuster.

00:04:30.788 --> 00:04:32.665
You know, I've picked very
unusual kind of stories.

00:04:32.665 --> 00:04:34.698
So, even I didn't expect
them to be successful.

00:04:34.698 --> 00:04:35.531
- [Interviewer] Do you feel pressure?

00:04:35.531 --> 00:04:36.432
Because you had this really long run,

00:04:36.432 --> 00:04:38.048
apart from anyone else,

00:04:38.048 --> 00:04:39.416
of success-
- Well, not really,

00:04:39.416 --> 00:04:40.400
because I feel that, you know,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.450
I'm not even thinking about that.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:42.490
I'm not even thinking about that.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.177
I just want to enjoy my work,

00:04:44.177 --> 00:04:46.195
and I want to surprise myself.

00:04:46.195 --> 00:04:48.624
Challenge myself and surprise my audience.

00:04:48.624 --> 00:04:50.502
And give them something new each time.

00:04:50.502 --> 00:04:51.335
So, I like doing that.

00:04:51.335 --> 00:04:52.731
I like doing different stuff.

00:04:52.731 --> 00:04:54.713
- When I look back today, after 25 years

00:04:54.713 --> 00:04:56.163
of being a professional,

00:04:56.163 --> 00:04:59.384
I think that that's one thing
that I feel happy about.

00:04:59.384 --> 00:05:00.760
That I lived on my terms.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.721
You see, today I'm successful.

00:05:01.721 --> 00:05:03.251
I may not have been successful.

00:05:03.251 --> 00:05:04.657
I may not have been successful.

00:05:04.657 --> 00:05:06.406
I didn't know I was
going to be successful.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.435
But I'm happy that I lived on my terms.

00:05:09.435 --> 00:05:10.738
And I'm happy that I never compromised.

00:05:10.738 --> 00:05:13.872
Whenever I was offered
something I was not happy with,

00:05:13.872 --> 00:05:14.705
I didn't do it.

00:05:14.705 --> 00:05:16.560
- Do you think you're the kind of person

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.758
or individuality, that follows his heart?

00:05:19.758 --> 00:05:20.960
- I do follow my heart.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.877
I don't think too much.

00:05:26.285 --> 00:05:28.681
I like to go instinctively.

00:05:28.681 --> 00:05:29.820
If I love something,

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:30.892
I want to do it.

00:05:30.892 --> 00:05:32.187
I don't think after that.

00:05:32.187 --> 00:05:34.687
So, in this film I had to play

00:05:36.582 --> 00:05:38.839
an older man, who's fat.

00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:41.206
Who's got gray hair, and who's aging.

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:44.355
And he's got four daughters.

00:05:44.355 --> 00:05:45.272
If I think,

00:05:46.757 --> 00:05:49.244
logically, then I should
not do a role like this

00:05:49.244 --> 00:05:51.023
for some time.

00:05:51.023 --> 00:05:52.449
But I love this film,

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:53.282
so I'm an actor.

00:05:53.282 --> 00:05:55.291
I play different roles.

00:05:55.291 --> 00:05:56.918
So I like to go with my heart,

00:05:56.918 --> 00:05:58.093
but I have to say that a lot

00:05:58.093 --> 00:05:59.811
of people are also successful when,

00:05:59.811 --> 00:06:01.207
those who go with their mind.

00:06:01.207 --> 00:06:02.265
There are no rules, I think.

00:06:02.265 --> 00:06:04.500
Each one makes their own path.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.697
But I like to follow my heart.

00:06:05.697 --> 00:06:07.674
It's not just the emotion of wanting

00:06:07.674 --> 00:06:09.297
to do something for somebody else,

00:06:09.297 --> 00:06:10.595
which is in itself a good emotion.

00:06:10.595 --> 00:06:11.428
- Yeah.

00:06:11.428 --> 00:06:12.874
- That you want to do
something for someone.

00:06:12.874 --> 00:06:16.780
But if you feel that your life
is incomplete if you don't.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:17.613
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:06:17.613 --> 00:06:19.217
- So you're doing it for yourself, really.

00:06:19.217 --> 00:06:20.050
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.249
- Of course, you're doing
it for someone else.

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:23.194
But I think that that's what is important,

00:06:23.194 --> 00:06:24.348
and it's something that happens to you

00:06:24.348 --> 00:06:25.692
if you feel like.

00:06:25.692 --> 00:06:27.318
It doesn't have to happen to you.

00:06:27.318 --> 00:06:29.393
But I think in me what
grew was this feeling

00:06:29.393 --> 00:06:32.641
that I needed to, for
myself, do something.

00:06:32.641 --> 00:06:35.513
That I felt better about myself

00:06:35.513 --> 00:06:36.849
when I felt I was..

00:06:36.849 --> 00:06:39.447
You know, I feel I'm so
privileged in so many ways.

00:06:39.447 --> 00:06:41.265
And I feel that, I really feel that

00:06:41.265 --> 00:06:44.233
when I see around me people
who are not as privileged,

00:06:44.233 --> 00:06:47.315
I can't just sit by and
be comfortable with that.

00:06:47.315 --> 00:06:49.398
There's a need in me to,

00:06:49.398 --> 00:06:53.148
you know, reach out and
perhaps help if I can.

00:06:53.148 --> 00:06:55.545
- And in a way, you're
lucky to have a position

00:06:55.545 --> 00:06:56.864
where people will listen.

00:06:56.864 --> 00:06:57.697
You'll be able to...

00:06:57.697 --> 00:07:00.974
- And I'd like to use it to
the best of my abilities.

00:07:00.974 --> 00:07:03.527
So I guess that's why I've moved
into the space that I have.

00:07:03.527 --> 00:07:06.362
It's for my own emotional or mental

00:07:06.362 --> 00:07:08.193
piece of mind and satisfaction.

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:10.722
- I don't do too much
to look after myself.

00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:12.349
But what I do, for sure,

00:07:12.349 --> 00:07:14.504
is I follow a very strict diet.

00:07:14.504 --> 00:07:16.418
And I think that has
made a huge difference

00:07:16.418 --> 00:07:19.751
to the way I feel and to the way I look.

00:07:20.853 --> 00:07:23.191
It has made me realize
that we are what we eat.

00:07:23.191 --> 00:07:24.854
- Absolutely.

00:07:24.854 --> 00:07:27.331
- So, I follow a very
healthy, balanced diet.

00:07:27.331 --> 00:07:28.833
I drink a lot of water.

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:30.285
- Yeah, we've seen that.

00:07:30.285 --> 00:07:33.063
- So, I think I drink about,
at least three liters a day.

00:07:33.063 --> 00:07:34.454
Sometimes four.

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:35.884
So I think what has happened is that

00:07:35.884 --> 00:07:38.134
because of my healthy diet,

00:07:40.017 --> 00:07:41.046
I sleep eight hours.

00:07:41.046 --> 00:07:45.129
- And I think success,
like Phunsukh Wangdu says,

00:07:46.559 --> 00:07:48.151
"Don't chase success.

00:07:48.151 --> 00:07:49.935
Chase excellence, and
success will come with it."

00:07:49.935 --> 00:07:52.340
So, I hope that I'm trying to do that.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.315
It is I'm trying to do that.

00:07:53.315 --> 00:07:54.167
I don't know that I achieve that,

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:56.981
But I'm trying to do that, yeah.

00:07:56.981 --> 00:07:58.239
This is a fascinating thing.

00:07:58.239 --> 00:08:00.799
Right through my life.

00:08:00.799 --> 00:08:03.563
Every important decision of mine.

00:08:03.563 --> 00:08:05.151
All the people who are important to me,

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:07.388
and who are close to
me, have always told me,

00:08:07.388 --> 00:08:08.692
"You're making a mistake.

00:08:08.692 --> 00:08:09.952
Don't do this."

00:08:09.952 --> 00:08:10.785
I'm always being told that.

00:08:10.785 --> 00:08:12.287
- [Interviewer] So
that's a good benchmark.

00:08:12.287 --> 00:08:13.549
- No.

00:08:13.549 --> 00:08:15.081
I appreciate the fact that people

00:08:15.081 --> 00:08:16.862
who are close to me
are concerned about me.

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:18.410
I appreciate the fact
that they care for me

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.157
and are worried for me.

00:08:20.157 --> 00:08:23.444
But what I've always
been happy about myself

00:08:23.444 --> 00:08:26.338
is that I've always
done what I believed in.

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:28.128
So I'll give you three examples.

00:08:28.128 --> 00:08:30.242
When I was in the 12th,

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:31.446
that's when I decided that I wanted

00:08:31.446 --> 00:08:34.950
to learn about filmmaking and cinema.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.695
So I told my family, my friends.

00:08:36.695 --> 00:08:37.639
Everyone around me that, you know

00:08:37.639 --> 00:08:39.668
I'm going to start working
as an assistant director

00:08:39.668 --> 00:08:41.698
and start learning about filmmaking.

00:08:41.698 --> 00:08:43.597
Everybody I knew at that time,

00:08:43.597 --> 00:08:46.118
my parents, of course, freaked out.

00:08:46.118 --> 00:08:46.968
You don't want to be a graduate?

00:08:46.968 --> 00:08:47.904
You want to leave your studies?

00:08:47.904 --> 00:08:49.772
It was (foreign language).

00:08:49.772 --> 00:08:51.721
And my uncles and aunts,

00:08:51.721 --> 00:08:53.209
they were all like, "You
know you can't do this."

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:54.225
My cousins.

00:08:54.225 --> 00:08:56.271
People my age, who I
thought would understand me.

00:08:56.271 --> 00:08:57.879
My friends said,

00:08:57.879 --> 00:09:00.743
(foreign language)

00:09:00.743 --> 00:09:01.576
"Do what you want.

00:09:01.576 --> 00:09:02.587
You want to be an actor,
you want to be a filmmaker.

00:09:02.587 --> 00:09:03.531
Do what you want.

00:09:03.531 --> 00:09:04.853
But at least be a graduate.

00:09:04.853 --> 00:09:06.041
It didn't make sense to me.

00:09:06.041 --> 00:09:07.260
I was like, why?

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.192
If I want to be a doctor,

00:09:08.192 --> 00:09:10.382
do I study commerce?

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.880
No, I study medicine.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:13.485
If I want to be an engineer,

00:09:13.485 --> 00:09:14.327
I study engineering.

00:09:14.327 --> 00:09:15.365
If I want to be a filmmaker,

00:09:15.365 --> 00:09:16.581
I want to study filmmaking.

00:09:16.581 --> 00:09:18.418
Why on earth should I waste time

00:09:18.418 --> 00:09:20.087
studying something else

00:09:20.087 --> 00:09:22.613
when I'm really clear
that this is my goal?

00:09:22.613 --> 00:09:23.588
So, no no.

00:09:23.588 --> 00:09:24.644
Because you need a paper

00:09:24.644 --> 00:09:26.307
which says you're a graduate.

00:09:26.307 --> 00:09:28.166
That was told to me.

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:29.690
I said, "No, I don't need a paper."

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:30.953
I don't need someone to tell me

00:09:30.953 --> 00:09:31.953
what I know.

00:09:33.003 --> 00:09:34.498
I know what I know.

00:09:34.498 --> 00:09:35.331
And if I need to know something,

00:09:35.331 --> 00:09:36.998
I'll learn about it.

00:09:38.628 --> 00:09:39.461
So I was very clear

00:09:39.461 --> 00:09:40.955
that this is what I want to do.

00:09:40.955 --> 00:09:42.135
So I didn't listen to anyone.

00:09:42.135 --> 00:09:43.074
I didn't listen to my friends,

00:09:43.074 --> 00:09:43.920
I didn't listen to my family.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.196
I just did what I wanted to do.

00:09:45.196 --> 00:09:46.255
Because I feel that,

00:09:46.255 --> 00:09:47.985
if I'm clear about what
I want to do, and I'm

00:09:47.985 --> 00:09:49.494
honest about it,

00:09:49.494 --> 00:09:51.577
and I'm sincere about it.

00:09:52.579 --> 00:09:54.971
And the reasons why I'm doing it is,

00:09:54.971 --> 00:09:56.075
is clear to me,

00:09:56.075 --> 00:09:58.658
then I must follow my instinct.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:02.410
Even if I have to go wrong tomorrow,

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.541
I'd rather go wrong on my instincts.

00:10:04.541 --> 00:10:05.511
I don't want to go wrong on

00:10:05.511 --> 00:10:07.553
somebody else's advice.

00:10:07.553 --> 00:10:09.691
If I've taken a wrong
step, I'll deal with it.

00:10:09.691 --> 00:10:10.524
I'll learn.

00:10:10.524 --> 00:10:12.003
It could be a learning experience for me.

